1154
01:55:39.420 --> 01:55:41.780
I was hungry and you gave me food.

1155
01:55:42.380 --> 01:55:44.460
I was sick and you visited me.

1156
01:55:44.660 --> 01:55:46.360
I was naked and you clothed me.

1157
01:55:47.500 --> 01:55:50.120
And Jesus is not just talking about

1158
01:55:50.120 --> 01:55:52.820
the nakedness of the body,

1159
01:55:54.300 --> 01:55:56.940
but to be naked spiritually.

1160
01:55:56.940 --> 01:55:57.200
me.

1161
01:56:00.000 --> 01:56:05.400
there is so much that the church gives to us to prepare us for the coming of Lent.

1162
01:56:05.800 --> 01:56:10.400
And then on the following Sunday, pre-Lenten Sunday, was the Forgiveness Sunday,

1163
01:56:11.280 --> 01:56:19.600
where we are told about the significance of forgiveness. We all have heard the Lord said,

1164
01:56:19.860 --> 01:56:26.280
in the measure that you forgive one another, I will forgive you. And that is critical for

1165
01:56:26.280 --> 01:56:28.200
Christians to understand this.

1166
01:56:30.000 --> 01:56:37.760
that you forgive others, I will forgive you. Again, that has to do with our relationship with

1167
01:56:37.760 --> 01:56:47.380
one another. And this the church emphatically proclaims, emphatically proclaims the forgiveness

1168
01:56:47.380 --> 01:56:55.340
of sins. And then the very next day we embark on the Lenten journey. And the first Sunday we came

1169
01:56:55.340 --> 01:56:58.740
to the first Sunday of Lent, the Sunday of Orthodoxy.

1170
01:57:00.000 --> 01:57:05.400
where we are commemorating the historical restoration of icons in the church.

1171
01:57:06.420 --> 01:57:13.420
But the church also reminds us of the present importance of that feast,

1172
01:57:13.940 --> 01:57:18.200
and that is the restoration of the image of God that is in all of us.

1173
01:57:19.200 --> 01:57:23.640
All of us are icons of Jesus Christ.

1174
01:57:23.640 --> 01:57:29.980
There is an icon just as our church&#x27;s walls and ceilings are beautified with.

1175
01:57:30.000 --> 01:57:38.060
icons. Each and every one of us possesses the image of God within us. But because of our

1176
01:57:38.060 --> 01:57:47.400
indifference to God, because of the sins that we have committed, that image of God becomes distorted.

1177
01:57:48.180 --> 01:57:55.760
It&#x27;s like a mosaic that has fallen and is broken into pieces. And it is through prayer and fasting

1178
01:57:55.760 --> 01:57:59.980
and repentance and all the things that the pre-Lenten Sunday...

1179
01:58:00.000 --> 01:58:07.800
showed us, introduced to us, and by God&#x27;s grace, that mosaic, that beautiful icon of Christ that

1180
01:58:07.800 --> 01:58:16.080
is in us, gradually becomes restored. And then we come to the second Sunday of Lent,

1181
01:58:16.280 --> 01:58:23.180
St. Gregory Palamas, the great father among the fathers of the church who taught us about prayer,

1182
01:58:23.180 --> 01:58:26.180
about how through prayer

1183
01:58:26.180 --> 01:58:29.980
we can obtain and have access to the grace.

1184
01:58:30.000 --> 01:58:41.620
grace of God to the point that we would not only be able to see the uncreated light of God,

1185
01:58:41.820 --> 01:58:52.360
but that it would illumine us as well. Fascinating. And prayer, St. Gregory talked about prayer that

1186
01:58:52.360 --> 01:58:57.660
was not with words, but prayer that was silence.

1187
01:59:00.000 --> 01:59:06.580
St. Gregory talked about the importance of stillness of the mind, stillness of the heart.

1188
01:59:07.240 --> 01:59:14.320
Remember, if we are talking at the same time, we can&#x27;t hear each other. We can&#x27;t listen to each

1189
01:59:14.320 --> 01:59:22.320
other. Likewise, when we say our prayers, St. Gregory teaches us, after you have said what

1190
01:59:22.320 --> 01:59:29.400
you&#x27;ve said, be silent. Be still and let God, let God speak to you.

1191
01:59:30.000 --> 01:59:37.400
experience his presence, his overwhelming peace that is filled with grace.

1192
01:59:39.240 --> 01:59:45.020
And then we commemorated the following Sunday, the Sunday of the veneration of the Holy Cross.

1193
01:59:45.520 --> 01:59:52.820
The cross is that quintessential symbol of Christianity. It reminds us of God&#x27;s

1194
01:59:52.820 --> 01:59:59.960
infinite power, power over death, because it was through the cross, his death.

1195
02:00:00.000 --> 02:00:07.700
on the cross, Jesus&#x27; death on the cross, that he was able to destroy death for us.

1196
02:00:08.900 --> 02:00:14.540
And through his death, resurrection, and promises resurrection to all of us.

1197
02:00:14.840 --> 02:00:21.020
The Holy Cross sits on the altar every day throughout the year. And there are just three

1198
02:00:21.020 --> 02:00:25.860
occasions during the church year that it is brought out in the midst of the people,

1199
02:00:25.860 --> 02:00:29.680
so that they may take courage and strength, that they may continue.

1200
02:00:30.000 --> 02:00:38.320
the rigors of the fast. Then last Sunday we commemorated St. John of the Ladder,

1201
02:00:38.460 --> 02:00:45.020
who wrote this beautiful work, The Ladder of Divine Ascent, of which Father Michael spoke

1202
02:00:45.020 --> 02:00:54.180
so beautifully last Sunday. He likened St. John of the Ladder, likened this journey through life

1203
02:00:54.180 --> 02:00:57.260
as really like climbing a ladder,

1204
02:00:57.260 --> 02:00:59.980
and every rung on the ladder is a...

1205
02:01:00.000 --> 02:01:01.740
a vice that needs to be overcome,

1206
02:01:02.020 --> 02:01:03.820
and a virtue to be attained.

1207
02:01:04.860 --> 02:01:06.100
30 rungs.

1208
02:01:06.660 --> 02:01:08.460
And once we get to the top,

1209
02:01:08.740 --> 02:01:13.660
we&#x27;ll experience what the church knows as theoses.

1210
02:01:14.500 --> 02:01:18.160
That is, vision of God.

1211
02:01:19.280 --> 02:01:20.600
Vision of God.

1212
02:01:23.360 --> 02:01:25.760
As Jesus said in the Beatitudes,

1213
02:01:25.960 --> 02:01:27.800
blessed are the pure in heart,

1214
02:01:28.840 --> 02:01:29.980
for they shall see.

1215
02:01:30.000 --> 02:01:37.240
see God. And today in our church, on the last Sunday of Lent, we commemorate St. Mary of Egypt,

1216
02:01:38.320 --> 02:01:50.740
a woman who in her early life probably surpassed every other person that ever lived in a sinful

1217
02:01:50.740 --> 02:01:58.280
life. She was someone who left home and lived on the streets of Alexandria at the age of 12.

1218
02:01:58.280 --> 02:01:59.920
and

1219
02:02:00.000 --> 02:02:07.560
she was so consumed by lust. There are some authors that called her a prostitute, but she

1220
02:02:07.560 --> 02:02:16.000
wasn&#x27;t a prostitute because she sought the pleasures of her flesh, of her body, and didn&#x27;t

1221
02:02:16.000 --> 02:02:24.560
want any money for it. A prostitute does what she does because she gets paid and needs the money.

1222
02:02:24.560 --> 02:02:29.460
St. Mary of Egypt was plying her trade.

1223
02:02:30.000 --> 02:02:36.120
without getting paid. She didn&#x27;t want to be paid. She did it purely for physical lust.

1224
02:02:37.480 --> 02:02:42.660
And when she heard, she was from Alexandria, Egypt, when she heard that there was a pilgrimage

1225
02:02:42.660 --> 02:02:51.240
to Jerusalem to see the Holy Cross of Christ that was going to be presented to all the faithful,

1226
02:02:51.660 --> 02:02:56.660
there was a pilgrimage. All these people boarded the ship in Alexandria and were on their way to

1227
02:02:56.660 --> 02:02:59.900
Jerusalem. Mary of Egypt also wanted

1228
02:03:00.000 --> 02:03:09.280
to board, but she had no money. So she essentially gave herself to the crew and passengers to do

1229
02:03:09.280 --> 02:03:16.480
with her what they pleased, just so she can go to Jerusalem. And when she arrived,

1230
02:03:17.920 --> 02:03:24.620
she followed the people to the church of the Holy Sepulchre. And when she wanted to go into the

1231
02:03:24.620 --> 02:03:29.760
church there was a force that was prohibiting her from entering.

1232
02:03:30.000 --> 02:03:36.060
church. No matter how much she tried, she couldn&#x27;t enter the church. And off to the side,

1233
02:03:36.120 --> 02:03:44.140
she saw an icon of the Virgin Mary and the Christ child. And she fell on her knees and prayed to the

1234
02:03:44.140 --> 02:03:52.540
Virgin Mary. She repented. She goes, I promise I just want to come inside the church and see the

1235
02:03:52.540 --> 02:03:57.360
cross of our Savior. And if you permit me, I will dedicate my life to you.

1236
02:04:00.000 --> 02:04:04.140
After a short while, she rose and entered into the church,

1237
02:04:04.960 --> 02:04:07.320
was able to see the precious cross.

1238
02:04:07.660 --> 02:04:09.800
And immediately after leaving the church,

1239
02:04:10.000 --> 02:04:12.720
she went out into the Palestinian desert.

1240
02:04:14.000 --> 02:04:17.700
And she lived there for 47 years in the desert

1241
02:04:17.700 --> 02:04:20.380
without seeing a single soul.

1242
02:04:21.600 --> 02:04:25.760
Until one year in her 46th year,

1243
02:04:26.020 --> 02:04:29.220
she encountered a priest by the name of Father Zosimas.

1244
02:04:30.540 --> 02:04:38.120
who he couldn&#x27;t believe seeing this emaciated, weather-beaten woman living in the desert.

1245
02:04:39.500 --> 02:04:43.480
And when he encountered her, he thought at first that she was a demon.

1246
02:04:45.400 --> 02:04:49.860
And then when he saw her do the sign of the cross, well, he knew she wasn&#x27;t a demon.

1247
02:04:50.060 --> 02:04:54.860
So he approached, and then he didn&#x27;t even realize that she was a woman.

1248
02:04:56.360 --> 02:04:59.900
and he fell on his feet and he fell on his knees.

1249
02:05:00.000 --> 02:05:05.920
and began asking this holy person to give her a blessing.

1250
02:05:06.800 --> 02:05:12.280
But she in turn fell on her feet and asked Father Zosimas for a blessing.

1251
02:05:14.080 --> 02:05:17.240
And so they had this dialogue.

1252
02:05:19.320 --> 02:05:23.500
Father Zosimas was amazed that she knew the scriptures by heart

1253
02:05:24.540 --> 02:05:26.800
without ever having read them,

1254
02:05:26.800 --> 02:05:29.980
without ever having heard the scripture.

1255
02:05:30.000 --> 02:05:37.820
scriptures. How is it that she was in the wilderness and that she was able to know about

1256
02:05:37.820 --> 02:05:42.720
Jesus Christ? She could quote the Psalms, she could quote the Old Testament prophets

1257
02:05:42.720 --> 02:05:50.320
and the New Testament. And clearly, Father Zosima said, what she could not read or did

1258
02:05:50.320 --> 02:05:57.660
not have access to read, this was told to her directly by God, and especially the Virgin Mary.

1259
02:05:57.660 --> 02:05:59.980
and

1260
02:06:00.000 --> 02:06:04.120
And so she told Father Zosimas to return in a year

1261
02:06:05.200 --> 02:06:07.580
and to bring with him Holy Communion

1262
02:06:07.580 --> 02:06:11.040
because she hadn&#x27;t received Holy Communion in 47 years.

1263
02:06:12.020 --> 02:06:14.760
And she says, come on Holy Thursday.

1264
02:06:16.120 --> 02:06:19.380
And Father Zosimas does exactly what she says.

1265
02:06:19.660 --> 02:06:20.640
A year passes.

1266
02:06:20.940 --> 02:06:23.460
He goes, sees her, gives her Communion.

1267
02:06:23.920 --> 02:06:27.220
And then she told him to return again the next year.

1268
02:06:27.220 --> 02:06:29.780
and when Father Zosimas returns

1269
02:06:30.000 --> 02:06:37.740
he didn&#x27;t even know her name. When he returned a year after, she had already died. And there was

1270
02:06:37.740 --> 02:06:47.340
an inscription in the sand that said, my name is Mary, I am from Egypt, and I died the day you gave

1271
02:06:47.340 --> 02:06:56.220
me Holy Communion. So she is honored in the Orthodox Church on the fifth Sunday of Lent,

1272
02:06:57.040 --> 02:06:59.700
reminding us, and on April 1st,

1273
02:07:00.000 --> 02:07:07.740
reminding us that no matter how sinful our life has been, there is always salvation,

1274
02:07:08.100 --> 02:07:16.560
redemption in Jesus Christ our Lord. Don&#x27;t ever say to yourself, I am hopeless. I am helpless

1275
02:07:16.560 --> 02:07:24.260
or beyond redemption. I&#x27;m sure if Mary of Egypt were here right now, which in a way she is,

1276
02:07:24.780 --> 02:07:29.920
she would tell each and every one of you never lose hope in the great

1277
02:07:30.000 --> 02:07:39.620
salvation and the works that Jesus Christ does. He worked a miracle in her life and

1278
02:07:39.620 --> 02:07:47.620
he awaits to work a miracle in our own. Never lose hope. Never be overwhelmed by

1279
02:07:47.620 --> 02:07:53.880
the many or how great your sins. Move forward by the grace of God, by the

1280
02:07:53.880 --> 02:07:56.100
intercessions of this holy mother

1281
02:07:57.480 --> 02:07:58.940
Mary of Egypt

1282
02:07:58.940 --> 02:07:59.980
and for all

1283
02:08:00.000 --> 02:08:03.720
all the saints and the angelic hosts as our intercessors.

1284
02:08:04.120 --> 02:08:08.680
May God bless and always keep you strong in his grace.

1285
02:08:08.980 --> 02:08:09.500
Amen.

1286
02:08:10.540 --> 02:08:11.800
May we all please rise.

1287
02:08:21.900 --> 02:08:26.040
And grant that, always guarded by your power,

1288
02:08:26.080 --> 02:08:28.300
we may give glory to you,

1289
02:08:28.300 --> 02:08:29.760
the Father

1290
02:08:30.000 --> 02:08:32.440
and the Son and the Holy Spirit

1291
02:08:32.440 --> 02:08:34.800
now and forever

1292
02:08:34.800 --> 02:08:38.660
and to the ages of ages.

1293
02:08:47.580 --> 02:08:51.020
No one bound by worldly desires and pleasures

1294
02:08:51.020 --> 02:08:53.480
is worthy to approach, draw near,

1295
02:08:53.600 --> 02:08:55.120
minister to you, the King of glory.

1296
02:08:55.640 --> 02:08:57.660
To serve you is great and awesome

1297
02:08:57.660 --> 02:08:58.920
even for the heavenly powers,

1298
02:08:58.920 --> 02:08:59.980
but because of your inner...

1299
02:09:00.000 --> 02:09:01.440
and immeasurable love for us.

1300
02:09:02.780 --> 02:09:05.240
You became man without alteration or change.

1301
02:09:05.400 --> 02:09:07.680
You have served as our high priest and as Lord of all

1302
02:09:07.680 --> 02:09:10.060
and have entrusted to us the celebration

1303
02:09:10.060 --> 02:09:13.060
of this liturgical sacrifice without the shedding of blood.

1304
02:09:13.560 --> 02:09:15.980
For you alone, Lord our God, rule over all things

1305
02:09:15.980 --> 02:09:17.120
in heaven and on earth.

1306
02:09:17.520 --> 02:09:19.820
You are seated on the throne of the cherubim,

1307
02:09:19.920 --> 02:09:21.660
the Lord of the seraphim and the King of Israel.

1308
02:09:22.360 --> 02:09:24.600
You alone are holy and dwell among your saints.

1309
02:09:24.600 --> 02:09:26.220
You alone are good and ready to hear.

1310
02:09:26.780 --> 02:09:28.560
Therefore, I implore you, look upon me,

1311
02:09:28.560 --> 02:09:29.980
are sinful and unworthy, sir.

1312
02:09:30.000 --> 02:09:33.320
and cleanse my soul and heart from evil consciousness.

1313
02:09:33.900 --> 02:09:35.960
Enable me by the power of your Holy Spirit,

1314
02:09:36.260 --> 02:09:38.320
so that vested with the grace of priesthood

1315
02:09:38.320 --> 02:09:40.020
I may stand before your holy table

1316
02:09:40.020 --> 02:09:43.100
and celebrate the mystery of your holy and pure body

1317
02:09:43.100 --> 02:09:44.100
and your precious blood.

1318
02:09:44.420 --> 02:09:46.440
To you I come with bowed head and pray.

1319
02:09:46.580 --> 02:09:48.260
Do not turn your face away from me

1320
02:09:48.260 --> 02:09:50.540
or reject me from among your children,

1321
02:09:50.580 --> 02:09:52.860
but make me your sinful and unworthy servant,

1322
02:09:53.040 --> 02:09:54.820
worthy to offer you these gifts.

1323
02:09:55.280 --> 02:09:57.980
For you, Christ our God, are the offer and the offered,

1324
02:09:57.980 --> 02:09:59.980
the one who receives and is destroyed.

1325
02:10:13.380 --> 02:10:15.580
Υπότιτλοι AUTHORWAVE

1326
02:10:37.240 --> 02:10:39.120
Υπότιτλοι AUTHORWAVE

1327
02:11:04.280 --> 02:11:06.840
Αλληλούια, Αλληλούια, Αλληλούια, Αλληλούια.

1328
02:11:07.660 --> 02:11:13.780
Είτε χερομυριστικώς οι κονίζοντες και τους οποίοι άδεικον γρυσάγιων ή ομπροσάδοντες.

1329
02:11:14.580 --> 02:11:20.060
Πάστε την βιωτική να ποθώ μεθαμέριναν, ως τον βασιλέα των όλων υποδεξόμενοι

1330
02:11:20.060 --> 02:11:25.680
τες αγγελικές αλληλούια, Αλληλούια, Αλληλούια.

1331
02:11:28.400 --> 02:11:29.980
Ανάσταση, Χριστό, Θεα σαν να μας δώσουμε.

1332
02:11:30.000 --> 02:11:33.900
προσκυνήσουμεν Άγιον Κύριον Ιησούν τον μόνον αναμάρτητον

1333
02:11:33.900 --> 02:11:38.200
των Σταυρών Σου Χριστέ προσκυνούμεν και την Αγία Σου Ανάσταση

1334
02:11:38.200 --> 02:11:42.180
ενυνούμεν και δοξάζουμε. Συγκαρι Θεός ημών εκτός σου

1335
02:11:42.180 --> 02:11:45.960
όλου τον ομάζ σου ονομάζουμε. Βλέπετε πάντα Συπιστή

1336
02:11:45.960 --> 02:11:48.620
προσκυνήσουμε την του Χριστού Αγία Ανάσταση.

1337
02:11:48.980 --> 02:11:51.960
Η Βουγαρήλφια για τον Σταυρό χαρά με τον κόσμο

1338
02:11:51.960 --> 02:11:53.900
διαπαντώσουμε τον Βούλιο στον Κύριο

1339
02:11:53.900 --> 02:11:56.100
ενυνούμεν την Ανάσταση δεχνώ.

1340
02:11:58.140 --> 02:11:59.980
Αυτό το βόλμα είναι που μήνες τύριοι.

1341
02:12:00.000 --> 02:12:01.860
Θανά το θανά στον όλα εσένα.

1342
02:12:02.780 --> 02:12:09.020
Λέει σώμη ο Θεός και από το μέσος σου και από το πλήθος των εκτευμών σου εξάλιξε ο εντόν νόμημά μου.

1343
02:12:09.320 --> 02:12:13.700
Επι πλύον πύρομαι από της ανομίας μου και από της αμαρτίας μου καθαρισώνα.

1344
02:12:14.080 --> 02:12:18.800
Ό,τι την ανομία μου οικογενός σου και η αγιαμαρτή μου ονοποιώνει ο ίσκης για παντός.

1345
02:12:19.560 --> 02:12:26.740
Σήμανον ήμαρτον και τα πανερόν ονοποιών σου εγκλείσα, όπως αντικαίωθείς σαν τις λόγες σου και νικήσεις από κοινές θέσεις.

1346
02:12:26.740 --> 02:12:29.540
Υπότιτλοι AUTHORWAVE

1347
02:12:35.000 --> 02:12:58.740
Σας ευχαριστώ, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή, Καλή

1348
02:12:58.740 --> 02:12:59.980
Υπότιτλοι AUTHORWAVE

1349
02:13:03.900 --> 02:13:06.860
Από όλους με τη μεγαλία στους οδηγείους.

1350
02:13:07.900 --> 02:13:11.620
Αν αδελφέ και στους ευθύνσοντας, αδελφέ, σύγχωρισόντας,

1351
02:13:11.620 --> 02:13:27.480
αδελφέ, σύγχωρισόντας, αδελφέ, σύγχωρισόντας, αδελφέ, σύγχωρισόντας,

1352
02:13:27.480 --> 02:13:29.540
σταγόντα και δεύχει δετροχήλια.

1353
02:13:30.000 --> 02:13:37.760
Ανεύει ο Θεός εν αλλαλαγμού Κύριος εν φωνής αλπιγός.

1354
02:14:07.120 --> 02:14:12.160
The Lord is the Son of God.

1355
02:14:38.340 --> 02:14:39.740
Αμήν.

1356
02:15:00.000 --> 02:15:07.500
